%N A057202 Numbers k such that |2^k - 21| is prime.
%C A057202 Original name: Numbers n such that 2^n - 21 is prime.
%C A057202 The first four terms [under the original name] correspond to negative primes. Dropping them gives A096820. - _Joerg Arndt_, Oct 05 2012
%t A057202 Do[ If[ PrimeQ[ 2^n - 21 ], Print[ n ] ], {n, 1, 3000} ]
%o A057202 (PARI) is(n)=isprime(abs(2^n - 21)) \\ _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Aug 08 2016
